  "best_idea": "Validate a character build on the server against an allow-list and a fixed budget (stats 10-60 with one total, skills capped at 50 with a total of 100 or 120), and refuse with a reason instead of silently resetting.",
  "decision": "adapt",
  "decision_why": "Keep the server-side budget and allow-list validation, which fits server-verified rules and one ledger; change the silent resets (stats to 10/10/10, name to Generic Player, whole skill list dropped) into explicit refusals, count every granted point, and clip skin with the chosen race, because the donor's silent fallbacks would hide errors from a phone player.",
  "decision_status": "proposed",
  "acceptance": "On a 375-wide create screen the stat and skill totals read 'x of 90' and 'x of 100', Create stays disabled until they match, and a refused name shows its reason; a server test asserts that a build totalling 99 skill points or a skill of 51 is refused with skill-total or skill-cap, and that a name containing '!' or starting 'gm' is refused."
